# --- Godot ---
.godot/
*.import
export.cfg
build/
*.tmp
.import/

# export_presets.cfg is deliberately TRACKED (it was ignored until Phase 6).
# It is real, shared project config now — the Android preset's exclude list is
# the only thing keeping the MCP dev bridge, the spike sandboxes and 327 tools
# scripts out of the shipping APK, and that must not be a per-machine setting
# somebody silently lacks. Godot writes keystore paths and passwords to the
# SEPARATE export_credentials.cfg, which stays ignored below — but this file is
# still worth a glance before committing, because a "signing" field that ends up
# here is a leaked credential in a public repo.
export_credentials.cfg
*.keystore
*.jks

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- IDEs ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*.sublime-*

# --- OS ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Secrets / config ---
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.key
*.pem
secrets/
credentials/

# --- Music (licence provenance unrecorded) ---
# The six score tracks + the hub ambience were UNTRACKED on 2026-08-03 before the
# repo went public: nothing in the repo recorded where they came from, and
# docs/NEXT-SESSION.md flagged "settle before anything public".
#
# Nothing breaks without them. Music.gd loads by path at runtime and already
# treats a missing file as a normal answer (see its _preferred_path header), and
# no .tscn references them — the game simply runs silent on a fresh clone.
# The two music test suites DO expect the files and will fail without them.
#
# ⚠ These blobs remain in git HISTORY. Untracking stops them shipping in new
# clones of the tip; it does not erase them. A full purge needs a history
# rewrite, which has not been done.
godot-project/assets/audio/music/

# --- Capture output ---
# The 17 MB source GIF is the raw capture; clips/*_web.gif is the one the README
# embeds (GitHub will not render an image over ~10 MB).
clips/*.gif
!clips/*_web.gif

# --- Build outputs ---
dist/
out/
exports/

# --- Asset workspace (large source files; keep baked sprites tracked) ---
art-source/raw/
audio-source/raw/
*.aseprite~
*.psd~

# --- Raw asset-pack download staging (NOT used by the game; imported into
#     godot-project/ when needed). Keeps ~800MB of packs out of git history. ---
/Effects/
/Music/

# --- Logs / temp ---
*.log
logs/
tmp/

# --- Local AI / models ---
models/
.ollama/
*.gguf

# --- Node (in case we add tooling) ---
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# --- macOS specific (Aseprite users) ---
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# --- Local tooling (Claude Code session data, Godot editor binary) ---
.claude/
godot-engine/

# --- Local MCP config (machine-specific absolute paths) ---
.mcp.json
content/vo/out/
content/vo/bank/_decode.tmp.wav
content/vo/raw/

# --- Posts: the delivered videos and everything derived on the way to them ---
# The BANK is the artefact and it is committed; a rendered post is not. Each one
# is 10-25 MB, it is regenerated by one command, and no two shoots produce the
# same fight anyway — so keeping them would be carrying weight nobody can reuse.
# `content/music/` is likewise generated: `generate_battle_music.py` IS the track.
content/posts/
content/music/

# Social account list — profile names, never commit
content/targets.json
content/daily_accounts.json
content/posted.json
content/targets.flagship.json
content/targets.arena.json

content/daily_post.log

# Operational state written by the posting/optimising loop. Regenerated on every
# run and naming real accounts, so it follows content/posted.json's convention.
# `content/analytics/` is the deliberate exception and IS committed: the vendor's
# cache reaches back only 30 days, so accumulated snapshots cannot be rebuilt.
content/queue_order.json
content/ALERT.txt
content/daily_accounts.pre-multiplatform.bak.json

# Wrangler's local deploy cache. Machine state, not source.
.wrangler/
